// REJECTS: Unexpected token '{'. Valid alternatives: [',', ']']
//
// The complex constraint body is delimited by PARENS, inside a bracketed constraint list,
// on a class whose own body is BRACES. Three delimiter kinds within four lines, and the
// choice is not free at any of them.
//
// Note what the parser offers instead: ',' or ']' -- i.e. having read the constraint NAME
// it is willing to end the constraint there (the short `id: expr` form needs a ':' too,
// so the alternatives are the list separators). A hand-written parser that accepts either
// bracket style "because the intent is obvious" diverges silently; there is no ambiguity
// for it to trip over, so nothing ever fails to tell it.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::BraceConstraint
[
   c1
   {
      ~function: $this.code->length() > 2
   }
]
{
   code: String[1];
}
